Package: oneplus-erhai-wifi
Version: 1.6
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: network-manager, iw, iproute2, oneplus-erhai-firmware (>= 1.4)
Recommends: kmod
Description: WCN7860 WiFi policy for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Selects the mainline ath12k driver for the internal WCN7860 radio: the
 modprobe policy no longer blacklists ath12k and instead blacklists the
 cnss2/qcacld vendor stack (cnss2, wlan), so udev binds ath12k_pci to the
 PCIe endpoint at boot, the firmware from oneplus-erhai-firmware 1.4
 (ath12k/WCN7860/hw2.0) is downloaded, and NetworkManager takes over the
 wlp1s0 station as usual. The WCN7880 power calibration that ath12k does
 itself is untouched by any modprobe option.
 .
 Needs the 7.3.4 kernel line at +b6 or newer (the first release with the
 WCN7860 hw2.0 definition, the pwrctrl pwrseq 110e match and the three
 PCIe/GCC wake patches); older kernels have no driver for this radio and
 the ath12k firmware cannot be used by them.
 .
 The cnss2/qcacld backend is still shipped but no longer enabled:
 erhai-wcn-wifi.service, erhai-wcn-holdfloor.service,
 erhai-wcn-devcd.service, erhai-wifi-discover.service and their scripts
 (erhai-wcn-wifi.sh, erhai-wcn-recover.sh, save-wcn-devcd.sh,
 erhai-wifi-discover.sh, wl_drvcmd) plus the qcacld INI
 (WCNSS_qcom_cfg.ini, scan_mode_6ghz=0) remain on disk for a manual
 fallback: blacklist ath12k, unblacklist wlan/cnss2 and
 `systemctl enable --now erhai-wcn-wifi.service`. version 1.5 of this
 package is the last one that defaults to that backend.
